{
    "version":  "1.0",
    "id":  "settings-general",
    "name":  "GeneralSettings",
    "description":  "General settings tab within the runner Settings panel. Displays application-level preferences for startup behavior and workflow builder defaults. Contains two sections: \u0027Application\u0027 (Auto-load Last Configuration on Startup, Launch on System Startup) and \u0027Workflow Builder\u0027 (Include AI Summary in New Workflows). All three settings are boolean toggle switches that persist via Tauri IPC commands. Toggling uses optimistic UI updates with rollback on failure. The Launch on System Startup toggle is backed by the OS autostart mechanism (Windows Registry Run key, macOS LaunchAgent, Linux .desktop) and reconciles against the actual OS state after each toggle.",
    "metadata":  {
                     "tags":  [
                                  "settings",
                                  "general",
                                  "startup",
                                  "autostart",
                                  "workflow-builder",
                                  "toggle"
                              ]
                 },
